# CSS / Style Structure

## Core rules

1. Use **Theme_JMLLC001** tokens — not legacy `brand-*`, indigo, or one-off hex when a token exists.
2. Load order: theme → Tailwind → shared → page.
3. Shell chrome → `shared.css`. Page-only layout → `css/pages/…`.
4. Per page: prefer **page CSS** *or* Tailwind utilities for the same patterns — not both.
5. After token/config changes: `npm run build:tailwind:Theme_JMLLC001`.

## Stylesheet stack

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="…/theme/Theme_JMLLC001/Theme_JMLLC001.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="…/css/tailwind.Theme_JMLLC001.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="…/css/shared.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="…/css/pages/{area}/{page}.css"><!-- optional -->
```

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| Theme | Tokens + base (`--color-primary`, fonts) |
| Tailwind | Utilities from Theme_JMLLC001 config |
| Shared | pageShell (sidebar, tabs, drawer, notifs), cross-page utils |
| Page | One-page components only |

**Dashboard (Option A):** visuals in `css/pages/portal/index.css`; Tailwind only for layout (`flex`, `grid`, `gap`, `hidden`).

Login may skip `shared.css` (no shell) and use `css/pages/login.css`.

## Portal conventions

- **A — Page CSS:** complex single pages (dashboard semantic classes).
- **B — Tailwind HTML:** simple pages.
- **C — `@layer components`:** shared patterns across portal pages.

Do not define the same pattern in both page CSS and Tailwind components.

## Shared vs page

**Shared:** `.portal-side-nav`, `.bottom-tab-bar`, `.nav-drawer`, `.notif-panel`, `.skeleton`, `.badge-chip`, admin `#sideNav`.

**Page CSS:** one-file layouts (hero card, local grids). Not colors/fonts already in theme.

Shell pages need `#nav-placeholder`, `#footer-placeholder`, `#tabs-placeholder` + `shared.css`.

## Prefer theme utilities

`bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `bg-accent`, `bg-surface`, `border-border`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `font-headline`, `font-body`.

## Anti-patterns

- Legacy `tailwind.portal.css` on themed pages
- Shell styles duplicated in page CSS
- Editing compiled Tailwind by hand
- Inline `<style>` except tiny overrides

## Checklist

- [ ] Theme + Tailwind (+ shared if shell)
- [ ] Page CSS only if needed
- [ ] Theme utilities over hex / `brand-*`
- [ ] `theme-color` `#13366e`
- [ ] Rebuild Tailwind if config changes
